### Error Codes

Source: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/adaccount/insights

This section lists common error codes and their descriptions for the Facebook Graph API insights endpoint.

```APIDOC
## Error Codes

### Description
Common error codes and their descriptions for the Insights API.

### Errors
- **200** - Permissions error
- **100** - Invalid parameter
- **3018** - The start date of the time range cannot be beyond 37 months from the current date
- **613** - Calls to this api have exceeded the rate limit.
- **2642** - Invalid cursors values
- **2635** - You are calling a deprecated version of the Ads API. Please update to the latest version.
- **190** - Invalid OAuth 2.0 Access Token
- **2500** - Error parsing graph query
- **105** - The number of parameters exceeded the maximum for this operation
- **3001** - Invalid query
```

### Page Insights > Requirements

Source: https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/insights

To successfully retrieve insights, the requester must use a Page access token generated by a user who has the ANALYZE task permission for the specific Page. Furthermore, the application must have the 'read_insights' and 'pages_read_engagement' permissions granted. Failure to specify at least one metric in the API request will result in an error response with code 3001, indicating that the request was incomplete.
